[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is **no** option struct, **no** setter, **no** mode enum, **no** global
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mutable state, **no** environment variable and **no** conditional compilation.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only `if`/`switch` in the whole library is the 4-conjunct guard in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `parse_val` (line 64) and the `if (parse_val(...))` in `driver` (line 75).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the configuration surface is entirely **input shape + struct state +
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m call sequence**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Public entry points (both must be driven directly)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | level | signature |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `run` | **low-level** — mutates a caller-owned `house_t`, prints 4 lines | `void run(house_t *, int)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `driver` | high-level one-shot wrapper — parses, builds `house_t{2,5,2.5}`, calls `run` **twice on the same struct** | `void driver(const char *)` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `house_t` is not in the public header but `run` takes it by pointer, so an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m external caller must reproduce the layout `{ int floors; int bedrooms; double
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bathrooms; }` (12 data bytes, 8-byte aligned, `sizeof == 16`). The tests
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m therefore also assert **struct layout/ABI agreement** by reading back the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mutated struct after `run` returns.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Input-shape axes the C actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `run`/`floors` (`int`): typical, 0, negative, `INT_MAX` (`++` wraps), `INT_MIN`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `run`/`bedrooms` (`int`): typical, 0, negative, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `run`/`bathrooms` (`double`), because of `+= 1.0` then `%.1f`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `k.0`, `k.5`, **`%.1f` round-half-to-even tie values** (`0.05 0.15 0.25 0.45
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   2.45 …`), negative, `-0.0`, `NaN`, `±inf`, magnitudes ≥ `1e17` where `+1.0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   is a no-op, `1e300` (309-char output), subnormal, `f64::MIN`/`MAX`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `run`/`extra_bedrooms` (`int`): 0, ±small, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, random
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **call sequence**: 1 call vs 2 calls vs N calls on the *same* struct — `run`
